<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="011" project="teams-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Teams SSO/NAA client auth strategy in the shared standalone-MSAL module</title>
    <phase>1 Shared Auth Module &amp; Host Adapter</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth, seamless workforce SSO correctness.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth, seamless workforce SSO correctness.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits shared auth module files from 010, serial.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>010</deps>
    <tags>auth, msal, teams</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add the Teams SSO/NAA strategy (Teams JS `getAuthToken` / nested app auth) to the shared standalone-MSAL module so the Teams host silently acquires a BFF-valid workforce token; the host selects the strategy.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Microsoft Teams JS SDK (`app.initialize`, `authentication.getAuthToken`, nested app auth/NAA), MSAL v5, and Microsoft Entra multitenant workforce apps. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    The shared standalone-MSAL module (task 010) exposes a Teams SSO/NAA acquisition path — using Teams JS `getAuthToken`/NAA against the workforce-multitenant authority — that silently yields a BFF-valid workforce token with no visible second login, alongside the unchanged CIAM path. The host (task 012) selects which strategy runs.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 001's foundation spike already proved Teams SSO/NAA can yield a BFF-valid workforce token end-to-end (systemuser + contact-only planes) and validated desktop/web behavior. This task productionizes that proven path as a selectable strategy inside the shared module from task 010, replacing throwaway spike code with the real implementation.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-auth.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-config.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <justification>
    <existing>`@spaarke/auth` strategies (Xrm/MSAL v3) and external-spa's CIAM MSAL v5 strategy.</existing>
    <extension>No — this is a new strategy inside the shared standalone-MSAL module (task 010), not an extension of `@spaarke/auth` or a fork of the CIAM strategy.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without this strategy, a Teams user cannot authenticate seamlessly via workforce SSO — they would face a double login or be blocked entirely, defeating D2 (workforce SSO, seamless, no second login).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 (Amendment A2)">SCOPE: the Teams SSO/NAA strategy inside `src/client/external-spa/src/auth/**`. Authenticate against the workforce-multitenant app (not CIAM); do NOT attempt CIAM sign-in inside Teams.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: token acquisition + BFF handoff only. Broker-only (NFR-02) — the acquired token authenticates to the BFF only and MUST NOT be exchanged downstream.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Teams SSO/NAA workforce token acquisition</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>projects/teams-app-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/teams-app-r1/design.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Pluggable-authority module" location="src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-config.ts">The workforce-multitenant authority shape added by task 010 — this task wires Teams JS `getAuthToken`/NAA acquisition against it.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Review task 001's spike findings (notes/spikes/foundation-spike-findings.md) for the proven Teams SSO/NAA acquisition sequence and any desktop/web quirks recorded.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the Teams SSO/NAA acquisition path in the shared module using Teams JS `app.initialize()` context + `getAuthToken`/NAA against the workforce-multitenant authority from task 010.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify the acquired token validates against the BFF's workforce default JwtBearer scheme with no second login prompt.</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm the CIAM strategy path is untouched and still functions (no cross-strategy regression).</step>
    <step order="5">Test in both Teams desktop and Teams web, noting any behavior difference against the spike's findings.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If Teams NAA/getAuthToken cannot yield a BFF-valid token as the task-001 spike expected (e.g., a regression from spike conditions, or new Conditional-Access blocking), STOP and escalate (root CLAUDE.md §6).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the external-spa client</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-auth.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Teams-hosted workforce user, when the Teams SSO/NAA strategy runs, then the Teams host acquires a BFF-valid workforce token with no second login.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the standalone SPA, when a CIAM user signs in, then it still uses the unchanged CIAM strategy (no cross-strategy regression).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The strategy is verified in both Teams desktop and Teams web.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an unauthenticated or consent-missing Teams caller, when the strategy runs, then the failure is surfaced to the caller (not silently degraded or retried into a broken state).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Builds directly on task 010's pluggable-authority module. Task 012 (host adapter) is the consumer that decides WHEN this strategy runs vs the CIAM strategy — this task only makes the strategy available and correct.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist. This is a FULL-rigor task (Step 9.5 gates apply).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
